      "id": "1998-01-24-oasis-longest-number-one",
      "date": "1998-01-24",
      "topic": "music",
      "text": "24 January saw Britpop titans **Oasis** climb to number one on the UK singles chart with *All Around the World*. Clocking in at an indulgent nine minutes and thirty-eight seconds, the sprawling orchestral epic set an enduring Guinness World Record as the longest single ever to top the British charts. Noel Gallagher unapologetically loaded the track with dozens of guitar overdubs and repeated key changes, apparently operating on the logic that more of everything was invariably better.",
      "wiki": "All Around the World (Oasis song)",
