      "date": "1998-02-07",
      "topic": "sport",
      "text": "7 February saw the opening ceremony of the **1998 Winter Olympics** in Nagano, Japan, featuring the Olympic debut of snowboarding and women's ice hockey. The games produced early high comedy when Canadian snowboarder Ross Rebagliati was stripped of his giant slalom gold medal after testing positive for minute traces of cannabis, claiming he had merely inhaled secondhand smoke at a party in Whistler. The IOC hastily restored the medal upon discovering that cannabis was not actually on their official list of banned substances.",
